Magic missile is a ranged attack. It is also (at higher levels)
*fearsomely* powerful.

At eighth level, each hit (and remember, it can hit multiple targets
and/or hit the same target multiple times, depending on the situation)
for 4-24 damage (average 14), at a time when most characters are doing
well to manage an per-blow average melee damage of 10.

At sixteenth level (readily achievable by the time you confront Rodney),
it hits for 8-48 damage (average 28), making each hit compare favorably
to Grayswandir and Frost Brand against ordinary monsters (with the
slight caveat that your melee attacks will never miss in the late game,
while your MMs can miss even if you are level 30).

At 30th level, it does 15-90 damage (average 52.5) per hit, making it
compare favorably to Grayswandir *against silver-hating monsters* and
meaning that it has a decent chance of defeating Death, Pestilence, or
Famine with a single hit.

If you're carrying the Knight quest artifact, those damage numbers are
doubled; even Demogorgon can be taken down with a single casting of MM
from a level 30 character with the Magic Mirror of Merlin if there's a
wall directly behind the purple '&'.
